course: dictionary
lesson: 3101
title: Eighteen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eighteen is the number 18, made of ten and eight. You can write it as a word or as the digits 18, and both mean the same amount. Count on from ten: eleven, twelve, thirteen, and so on up to eighteen.
explain: Eighteen can be split into equal groups. Because 18 = 2 × 9 and 18 = 3 × 6, you can share 18 sweets equally between 2 friends (9 each) or between 3 friends (6 each). Ask yourself which groups fit exactly with none left over.
explain: Look at the context: «A real cat has five toes on each front paw and four on each back paw, eighteen in all.» To check it, add the parts: 5 + 5 + 4 + 4 = 18. Adding the parts is a good way to check a big number.
fact: Eighteen is the number 18, ten and eight.
fact: 18 = 2 × 9 and 18 = 3 × 6, so 18 can be shared equally into 2, 3, 6 or 9 groups.
fact: «All insects have six legs and three body parts, so a beetle, an ant and a bee have eighteen legs together.»
fact: In many countries, at eighteen you count as a grown-up.
fact: A golf course usually has 18 holes.
exercise: What is eighteen written as digits? | 81 | 180 | *18 | 118
exercise: You share 18 sweets equally between 3 friends. How many does each friend get? | 3 | 5 | 9 | *6
exercise: «A real cat has five toes on each front paw and four on each back paw, eighteen in all.» How many toes are on the two front paws together? | *10 | 9 | 8 | 18
test: Which pair of numbers multiplies to make 18? | 4 × 4 | *3 × 6 | 5 × 5 | 2 × 8
test: In the UK, from what age can most people vote? | 10 | 21 | 16 | *18
exam: What is 9 + 9? | 81 | 19 | 17 | *18
